From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Link libcef with 16 KiB sections

Link libcef.dll with /ALIGN:16384 and /FILEALIGN:16384, so that every
section starts on a 16 KiB boundary in memory and in the file. Wine on
iOS maps an image section from the file (MAP_PRIVATE) only when both are
16 KiB-aligned, the host's page size; with 4 KiB sections and 0x200 file
alignment it reads all of libcef (246 MiB) into each process's private
memory, six copies in a Red Dead Redemption 2 play (PLA-415). Mapped from
the file, only the pages a process relocates or writes become its own.
lld-link warns that /ALIGN without /DRIVER may not run, and Chromium
links with /WX; the config comes after /WX and adds /WX:NO, so that
warning stays a warning. Apply to the CEF pin before its stock Chromium
patcher runs.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-19-shared-libcef.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 BUILD.gn | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/BUILD.gn b/BUILD.gn
index 6f653c8cc..c8fc79f9c 100644
--- a/BUILD.gn
+++ b/BUILD.gn
@@ -1123,6 +1123,19 @@
 # libcef_dll_wrapper static targets.
 #
 
+# Playport: sections aligned to 16 KiB in memory and in the file, so that a
+# host with 16 KiB pages (Wine on iOS) maps each section from the DLL file
+# instead of reading it into every process's private memory. lld-link warns
+# that /ALIGN without /DRIVER may not run; Windows and Wine load such a DLL,
+# so that warning alone is not fatal here (this config comes after /WX).
+config("playport_16k_sections") {
+  ldflags = [
+    "/ALIGN:16384",
+    "/FILEALIGN:16384",
+    "/WX:NO",
+  ]
+}
+
 # Configuration that will be applied to all targets that build autogen files.
 config("libcef_autogen_config") {
   if (is_clang) {
@@ -1793,6 +1806,10 @@
       # we need some DLLs loaded in child processes before sandbox lockdown.
       configs += [ "//build/config/win:delayloads" ]
 
+      # Playport: 16 KiB sections in memory and in the file, so a 16 KiB-page
+      # host can map them from the file and share their clean pages.
+      configs += [ ":playport_16k_sections" ]
+
       libs = [
         "comctl32.lib",
         # For D3D11_DECODER_PROFILE_H264_VLD_NOFGT.
